<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Béhanzin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1845–<a href="/years/1906">1906</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Behanzin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Béhanzin was the last independent king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a>, reigning from 1889 to 1894. He fought two wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> over its claims to the coast around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-novo">Porto-Novo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotonou">Cotonou</a>, but French forces under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-amedee-dodds">Alfred-Amédée Dodds</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abomey">Abomey</a> in 1892. He surrendered in 1894 and was exiled to Martinique and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, where he died. He is honoured as a national hero in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/behanzin.jpg" alt="Béhanzin" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexandre d'Albéca · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Behanzin-1895.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
